-- Retargeted from a historical rejection fixture by the unified derive / canonical evidence revision (2026-08-02).
-- Flipped reject -> accept: funExt is now a primitive portable-foundation principle
-- (Spec.md §11.4.1), and the baseline provider's h-level closure includes function and
-- dependent-function closure using funExt (§14.5.5 item 5; the prelude `piIsSet` shape),
-- so IsSet Int gives IsSet (Int -> Int) and structural h-level closure (§14.5.1
-- provider 2) lifts it through the single constructor. The type's "Unsupported..."
-- name and the fixture's original residence under negative/ are both stale; a residual
-- negative test in this family would need a field whose codomain genuinely lacks
-- IsSet (e.g. Int -> Type).

data UnsupportedFunctionField : Type =
    UnsupportedFunctionField
        (run : Int -> Int)

derive IsSet UnsupportedFunctionField

--! assertNoErrors

-- STATUS(3014a0d9): PASS after authenticated Pi IsSet closure.
